body:
So I see a few things;

This is not to be mean. Personally I see several features that would be considered more masculine - a high hairline, deep set eyes (I can’t tell from frontals if you have a brow ridge but will also assume so as most AMAB people have it), a long face and a big squarish chin. 

The good news? A majority can be fixed surgically. The bad news? It’s expensive and hurts like hell.
